<section id="other-numberings" title="Numberings for selected languages">
  <h1>Numberings for selected languages</h1>
  <p>
    <code>Numberer</code> implementations are available for several selected European languages, and
    you can use these as a prototype to write your own.</p>
  <p>In Saxon-PE/EE these numberers are used for the given languages only if the JAR file containing the ICU libraries
    is not available on the classpath. (This is a transitional arrangement for Saxon 9.6, to ease transition to ICU.
    This mechanism will probably be dropped in a later release.)
    These numberers are not built in with Saxon-HE, but are available as open source code, and it is possible
    to configure them by writing a subclass of <a class="javalink"
      href="net.sf.saxon.lib.LocalizerFactory">LocalizerFactory</a> and registering it with
    the <a class="javalink" href="net.sf.saxon.Configuration">Configuration</a>.</p>
