  <p>For English, the language codes <code>en-x-hyphen</code> and <code>en-x-nohyphen</code> can be used to control whether numbers in the range 21 to 99
  are spelled out with hyphen or space as a separator ("thirty-one" versus "thirty one"). By default, a hyphen is used for ordinal numbers, while a space
  is used for cardinal numbers.</p>

